error: the product has moved off round `r28-11-09-2026`: it pins 1fe415c0efe18c0f7a571481c6bf0c224bca42b2f5690d164b1b26bffef46630 and this tree is 6a91d022f7c7180774967f29fea2e9e30c4c78216c5ca63984213267bc9a0d8a. Every arm in a round runs against one revision , so this dispatch would put two revisions in one table. Either restore the tree, or close the round by opening the next one:
  uv run --no-sync python tools/bench/product.py --open <id> --opened <YYYY-MM-DD> --why "what this boundary is for" --adopted "#N what landed"
Opening a round re-baselines: arms measured under the old one are not comparable with arms measured under the new one, so every identity change waiting on a boundary lands in this one rather than in a round of its own .
